{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e04-scene-10",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Детектор лжи  (The Lie Detector)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "expert": "Эксперт",
  "fedya": "Федя"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The chef is determined to find the traitor, so he has hired a lie-detector expert and set up a machine in his office. Fedya, the fish cook, is the first to be questioned. Here is the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Заходи, Федя. Садись на стул.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, а что это такое?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это настоящий детектор лжи, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я должен поймать крысу на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Отвечайте только «да» или «нет».",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Хорошо, это мне вполне понятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Скажите, сегодня действительно среда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, сегодня среда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Ваше настоящее имя Фёдор?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ходил в соседний ресторан?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нет, я никуда не ходил.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Свободен. Позови сюда Сеню.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through the questioning.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Заходи, Федя. Садись на стул.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Come in, Fedya. Sit down on the chair.' \"Zakhodi\" is \"come in\", with \"za-\" for going inside. \"Sadis'\" is \"seat yourself\", with -s' for the self.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, а что это такое?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, what is this thing?' \"Chto eto takoye?\" is \"what is this such?\", a handy way to ask what something is.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это настоящий детектор лжи, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is a real lie detector, Fedya.' \"Lozh'\", a lie, drops its vowel in \"lzhi\", of a lie. The machine is \"detektor lzhi\", detector of a lie.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я должен поймать крысу на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I must catch the rat in the kitchen.' \"Krysa\", rat, is also Russian slang for a traitor. \"Poymat'\" is \"to catch\", and \"dolzhen\" is \"must\" for a man.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Отвечайте только «да» или «нет».",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Answer only yes or no.' \"Otvechayte\" is a command with the polite -te. \"Tol'ko\" is \"only\", and \"ili\" is \"or\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Хорошо, это мне вполне понятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fine, that is completely clear to me.' \"Vpolne\" is \"in full\", from \"polnyy\", full. \"Mne ponyatno\", to me it's clear, needs no \"I\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Скажите, сегодня действительно среда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Tell me, is today really Wednesday?' \"Sreda\", Wednesday, is related to \"seredina\", middle, since it falls mid-week. \"Deystvitel'no\" is \"really\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, сегодня среда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, today is Wednesday.' Fedya repeats \"sreda\" with no verb, because Russian leaves out \"is\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Ваше настоящее имя Фёдор?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Is your real name Fyodor?' \"Fyodor\" is the full name behind \"Fedya\". \"Nastoyashcheye\", real, ends in -eye because \"imya\", name, is neuter.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes.' Just \"da\", which is what the expert asked for.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ходил в соседний ресторан?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you go to the neighboring restaurant?' \"Khodil\" is \"went and came back\". \"Sosedniy\", neighbouring, is from \"sosed\", neighbour.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нет, я никуда не ходил.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I did not go anywhere.' \"Nikuda ne khodil\" is \"nowhere not went\", the double negative.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Свободен. Позови сюда Сеню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are free to go. Call Senya in here.' \"Svoboden\" is the man's short \"free\". \"Pozovi\" is \"call\", and \"Senya\" turns into \"Senyu\" as the one called. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Заходи, Федя. Садись на стул.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, а что это такое?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это настоящий детектор лжи, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я должен поймать крысу на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Отвечайте только «да» или «нет».",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Хорошо, это мне вполне понятно.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Скажите, сегодня действительно среда?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, сегодня среда.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Ваше настоящее имя Фёдор?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ходил в соседний ресторан?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нет, я никуда не ходил.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Свободен. Позови сюда Сеню.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Fedya passes the test and is sent to fetch Senya. The phrase to keep is \"detektor lzhi\", \"lie detector\", where \"lozh'\" is a lie.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
